<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The themed-icon layer (Android 13+), which the system recolours to the user's wallpaper
  palette. One colour: the launcher tints it, so any colour here is a placeholder. The walls are
  what carries the shape once the pawn and the bars are the same value, so the gap between them
  is left wide enough to survive the tint.

  This used to be the foreground's geometry with the shading taken out, and that sentence stood
  here until the icon became a photograph. It is now the last place in the icon set where the
  drawn mark survives — the background layer is the board itself and the foreground is a
  transparent path — so there is nothing left to keep it in step with except
  res/drawable/ic_notification.xml, which is the same idea reduced to what reads at the height
  of a status bar. Move one and the other has to move with it.
-->
